bilities UNC Charlotte is accepting applications for adjunct or part-time faculty. These positions are temporary and usually involve teaching a particular course or courses for a particular semester. These positions are temporary and do not accrue benefits. Responsibilities could include: Developing and/or updating course syllabus, preparation of lectures, projects, or other student assignments, meeting all designated class periods, maintaining regularly scheduled office hours, grading student assignments and exams in a timely manner, submitting completed mid-semester progress reports and final grades according to University regulations. Undergraduate Academic Programs include: Civil Engineering Technology Construction Engineering Construction Management Graduate Academic Program includes: Construction and Facilities Engineering, M.S. The University of North Carolina at Charlotte is an Equal Opportunity Employer and an ADVANCE Institution that strives to create an academic climate in which the dignity of all individuals is respected and maintained. Women, minorities, veterans and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, protected veteran status, or disability. The chosen applicant is subject to a criminal background check. Other Work/Responsibilities Necessary Licenses or Certifications Proposed Hire Date 01/04/2027 Contact Information Civil Engineering Technology – Don Chen (dchen9@charlotte.edu) Construction Engineering – Stephanie Pilkington (spilking@charlotte.edu) Construction Management – Wayne Goff (jgoff3@charlotte.edu) Construction and Facilities Engineering, M.S. – Jake Smithwick (jsmithw1@charlotte.edu) Expected Length of Assignment Spring 2027 Term and/or Summer 2027 Term Posting Open Date 10/05/2026 Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Notes to Applicants All finalists will be required to provide an offici