    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/71524": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Assistant Teaching Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Assistant Teaching Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit ● Cover Letter ● Curriculum Vitae ● Statement of Teaching Philosophy ● Honors syllabus or a short proposal for an interdisciplinary honors seminar ● Contact Information for three Professional References ● Additional application materials as requested through the University application system The candidate chosen for this position will be required to provide an official transcript of their highest earned degree and submit to a criminal background check. Position Information General Information Position Number 003888 Working Title Assistant Teaching Professor Classification Title 9-Mo Non-Tenure Track Faculty College Honors College (Adm) Department Honors College Position Designation Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per year 9 Primary Purpose of Department The Honors College is an academic and support hub for academically motivated UNC Charlotte undergraduates, including all members of honors programs, merit scholars, and students seeking endorsement for nationally competitive awards. Vacancy Open to All Candidates Description of Work The University of North Carolina at Charlotte recognizes the differentiation of mission, goals, and objectives inherent in the diversity of disciplines represented by its colleges and departments. Thus, the Job Responsibilities and Essential Functions for Non-Tenure Track Faculty should be interpreted in the context of the related departmental and collegiate teaching goals. Teaching – Faculty responsibilities and essential functions with respect to teaching may include but are not limited to: subject matter competence, course design, course presentation, and grading student work. If conducting or supporting research is an element of the work required in this position, then the following statement is applicable: This position is subject to research-security screening. As part of the application, applicants must disclose, either in their CV or in a separate document submitted with the application , all current appointments or affiliations with foreign institutions or organizations, foreign research support, and ongoing research collaborations with foreign institutions, organizations, or their personnel. Before candidates advance to an on-campus interview, the university will review this information and other publicly available information for relationships involving institutions on the current Section 1286 list and any other applicable U.S. restricted-party lists. A disclosed or identified relationship does not automatically disqualify a candidate. As a condition of employment, a selected candidate must resolve any relationship the university determines would violate applicable law or sponsor requirements or materially impair the candidate’s or the university’s eligibility for federal funding. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach 9 credit hours per semester in the Honors College. Maintain and progress on a research agenda resulting, on average, in one publication per year over a 3-year period. Conference presentations contribute to this effort. Engage in service activities equivalent to about 8 hours per week, on average, over the course of the semester. This includes attending Honors College staff meetings, honors student activities, and recruiting events. Minimum Experience/Education UNC Charlotte gives primary consideration to the earned masters and/or terminal degree in the teaching discipline or a related discipline. Preferred Education, Skills and Experience ● Graduate training that spans multiple disciplines and/or experience teaching interdisciplinary courses ● Demonstrated success teaching undergraduate students in honors, interdisciplinary, or related academic programs. ● Experience developing innovative, student-centered, and inclusive instructional practices. ● Evidence of effective student mentoring, advising, or coaching. ● Experience supporting undergraduate research, experiential learning, service-learning, or other high-impact educational practices. ● Ability to collaborate effectively with administrators, faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. ● Commitment to fostering academic excellence, leadership development, and student engagement among high-achieving students PhD Teaching high-performing college students. Necessary Licenses/Certifications Special Notes to Applicants Applicants should submit ● Cover Letter ● Curriculum Vitae ● Statement of Teaching Philosophy ● Honors syllabus or a short proposal for an interdisciplinary honors seminar ● Contact Information for three Professional References ● Additional application materials as requested through the University application system The candidate chosen for this position will be required to provide an official transcript of their highest earned degree and submit to a criminal background check. Job Open Date 10/27/2026 Job Close Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Date Review of Applications will Begin 01/15/2027 Proposed Hire Date 08/01/2027 If time-limited, please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Sample Syllabi Contact Information for References Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 9201 University City Blvd Charlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
